From: kevinbrar2024 <kevinbrar2024@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:47:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Keep conditional target binding outside reflexive
 triggers

Only preserve a clause's explicit typed target when its condition marks a separate reflexive trigger. Ordinary If-you-do-this-way clauses such as Cragganwick Cremator still bind their recipient to the enclosing ability, while When-you-do-this-way triggers such as Narset and Vivien keep their own target selection.\n\nRegression coverage includes Cragganwick's ParentTarget/runtime damage, Narset's printed reflexive target and discarded-card mana value, and Vivien's printed reflexive target and entering-creature power. Ambuscade, Bite Down on Crime, and Venom Blast remain the analogues for the unconditional one-sided-fight binder.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
